{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing GitHub issue #15 (backend split prefactor) in user/delegate. Read `gh issue view 15` and its comments (`gh issue view 15 --comments` — the orchestrator rulings are binding). Spec is #4. Follow AGENTS.md. Do not delegate further: no subagents, no delegate/cursor_run tools.\n\nWorking directory: this worktree, branch `15-backend-split`, based on origin/main 337c657. Stay on this branch; do not create branches.\n\n## Goal\nCursor stays the only backend and behaviour is unchanged, but nothing outside the cursor backend knows cursor-agent's flags or binary, and the job/finalize/output code consumes a normalized result instead of the raw cursor JSON.\n\n## Required shape\n1. An enum in `src/backends/mod.rs` selected by the model table's `backend` string. Literal signature:\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Backend {\n    Cursor,\n}\n\nimpl Backend {\n    /// None for a backend that is not implemented (pi, claude until #16/#17).\n    pub fn from_name(name: &str) -> Option<Backend>;\n    pub fn name(self) -> &'static str;\n    /// Resolved binary path (CURSOR_AGENT_BIN, then PATH, then ~/.local/bin).\n    pub fn bin(self) -> String;\n    /// Full argv (without the binary) and whether the run may write.\n    pub fn argv(self, model: &str, capability: Capability, session: Option<&str>, prompt: &str) -> (Vec<String>, bool);\n    /// Spawn and drive the child; same contract as today's `Backend::run`.\n    pub fn spawn(self, spec: &JobSpec) -> Spawned;\n}\n```\nEach method is a `match self { Backend::Cursor => cursor::... }`. No `dyn` trait for backend selection.\n\n2. The existing `trait Backend` in `src/backends/types.rs` is the job runner's test seam (src/job/tests.rs has `impl Backend for FakeBackend`). Rename that trait to `Runner` and keep it as the seam `JobDeps` holds; `Backend` (the enum) implements `Runner` by delegating to `spawn`. Job tests change only the trait name.\n\n3. Normalized result. Replace `BackendResult.raw: RawCursorJson` with normalized fields; `RawCursorJson` becomes private to the cursor parsing path (it may stay used by `src/stream.rs`, which stays at the crate root because #17's Claude parser will reuse it):\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default)]\npub struct BackendResult {\n    pub text: String,\n    pub session_id: Option<String>,\n    pub usage: Option<Usage>,\n    /// Cost the backend reported itself; None means price from the model table.\n    pub cost_usd: Option<f64>,\n    pub is_error: Option<bool>,\n    pub duration_ms: Option<f64>,\n    pub clean_exit: bool,\n    pub stderr: String,\n}\n```\n`finalize.rs`/`output.rs` use these fields; cost = `res.cost_usd` if Some (then `cost_estimated: false`), else `compute_cost` from the table as today (`cost_estimated: true`). STATUS-line parsing stays in `output.rs`.\n\nLiteral expected value for `tests/fixtures/cursor/plain-answer.stdout` with a clean exit and empty stderr:\n```rust\nBackendResult {\n    text: \"391\\n\\nSTATUS: DONE\".into(),\n    session_id: Some(\"54b96753-cec4-4820-ade9-aa49ebbb463a\".into()),\n    usage: Some(Usage { input_tokens: 9451.0, output_tokens: 72.0, cache_read_tokens: 3872.0, cache_write_tokens: 0.0, ..Default::default() }),\n    cost_usd: None,\n    is_error: Some(false),\n    duration_ms: Some(3279.0),\n    clean_exit: true,\n    stderr: String::new(),\n}\n```\n(Adjust only if `Usage` has other fields; check `src/types.rs`.)\n\n4. Move into the cursor backend (`src/backends/cursor.rs`, or `src/backends/cursor/` as a directory if it gets large): `build_argv`, `map_capability` (from `src/capability.rs` — delete the `allow_unsandboxed=false` path: the CLI always passes true, so read-write is `--sandbox disabled`), `resolve_cursor_bin` (from `src/cursor_bin.rs`), and the cursor-agent doctor probes from `src/doctor.rs` (`--version`, `about` parsing, `--list-models`/`models`). Delete the emptied files. `src/cli.rs` builds a job through `Backend::from_name(&entry.backend)` + `argv` + `bin` + `spawn`; it must no longer import anything cursor-specific. `src/cli_info.rs`/doctor dispatch through the enum (`from_name` None → the existing \"skip\"/\"not implemented\" behaviour).\n\n5. A pure parse entry the fixture tests and the live driver share, e.g. `cursor::parse_stdout(stdout: &str, clean_exit: bool, stderr: &str) -> BackendResult` built on `stream::parse_line`; the spawn driver uses the same finishing function so tests exercise production code. Rulings: unparseable lines are skipped; a clean exit with no `result` line is an error (`is_error: Some(true)`, text explains no result line); a non-clean exit with empty stdout (bad model) is an error whose text is the stderr tail; CANCELLED is set only by the supervisor, never the parser.\n\n## Tests\n- New `tests/cursor_fixtures.rs` (or a `#[cfg(test)]` module in the cursor backend reading via `env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")`): one test per `tests/fixtures/cursor/*.stdout`. Exit status is not stored in the fixtures; use this table: `error-bad-model` → exit 1 (clean_exit false, stderr from the `.stderr` file), `cancelled` → killed (clean_exit false), every other fixture → clean exit. Assert text/session/usage/is_error; for `plain-answer` assert the literal value above; for `tool-calls-fix` also assert that progress saw at least one tool call (run its lines through `parse_line` and check `last_tool`).\n- A test that iterates the directory and fails if a `.stdout` fixture has no case (so new fixtures can't be silently skipped) — or one table-driven test over every file with the exit table as the only per-file data. Prefer the latter (less code).\n- All existing tests pass; changes to existing tests limited to imports/renames (`Runner`, moved paths, `BackendResult` field access in finalize tests).\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` (includes tests/budgets.rs) must pass.\n\n## File fence\nOwns `src/` and `tests/` (except `tests/fixtures/` contents, read-only). Forbidden: skills/, README.md, .github/, scripts/, Cargo.toml dependencies (no new crates). A parallel lane edits skills/ only.\n\n## Finish\nCommit on `15-backend-split` (one or more commits; conventional messages ending `Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>`). Do not push.\n\nCompletion bar: report the commit SHA(s), the fmt/clippy/test summary (test counts), and `git grep -n -e '--print' -e 'stream-json' -e 'cursor-agent' -e 'CURSOR_AGENT_BIN' -- src | grep -v '^src/backends/'` output (must be empty or justified) — or a failure triage, nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, what you'd change (\"none\" is fine). End with a STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"1d546125-183e-46a3-aaab-e9734f91ce3e"}
