{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":1409339,"duration_api_ms":1409339,"is_error":false,"result":"I'll start by reading the issue, its binding comments, and the agent docs so the backend split matches the spec.The issue and spec are in. Next I’ll map the current backend, job, and CLI code so the enum and normalized result land in the right places.The split is clear: an enum selects the backend, the job seam stays a trait, and cursor-only details move behind it. I’ll start putting that shape in place.The argv test compared the wrong types. I’ll fix that while moving the doctor probes into the cursor backend.Commit `ec578493add39a5b9bd564fc443d7acb0c4e8f00` on `15-backend-split` (parent `337c657`). Not pushed.\n\n- `cargo fmt --check`: passed\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed\n- `cargo test`: 167 passed, 1 ignored (live). Lib 129, budgets 6, cli_e2e 27, cli_info_e2e 5.\n\nEncapsulation grep (`--print`, `stream-json`, `cursor-agent`, `CURSOR_AGENT_BIN` under `src/`, excluding `src/backends/`): empty.\n\n**Friction**\n- The plain-answer literal includes `..Default::default()` on `Usage`, but `Usage` has only those four fields, so clippy's `needless_update` rejects it. Dropped the `..`.\n- Job-test dummy argv used `--print` and `cursor-agent`, which the encapsulation grep flags outside `src/backends/`. Those two strings changed along with the `Runner` rename.\n- Doctor lines in `cli_info.rs` contained `cursor-agent`, so the human text moved with the probes. The issue comment's method list (`parse`, `resume_args`) also differs from the literal `spawn` / `argv` signature; followed the brief.\n\nSTATUS: DONE","session_id":"1d546125-183e-46a3-aaab-e9734f91ce3e","request_id":"a39a3dae-67ec-4300-bf85-501258a620a7","usage":{"inputTokens":232095,"outputTokens":95133,"cacheReadTokens":5452032,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
